## Current status

From the project docs and current app structure, the site is not fully completed yet. The repository is still in a rebuild/phase-based state rather than a finished production product. The clearest evidence is in project-state.md and PROJECT_REBUILD_PLAN.md.

## What is still incomplete

### 1) Admin dashboard features
These are only partly complete:
- The admin control plane is still described as a planned phase, not a fully finished system.
- Approval, moderation, and operational workflows are present in structure, but they are not fully production-ready end to end.
- Admin modules such as analytics, reporting, wallet management, support, permissions, and CMS are scaffolded, but the full live operational experience is still incomplete.
- The docs explicitly call out that full configurable admin controls, audit trails, and change history are still pending.

### 2) User interface and UX
The UI has a solid foundation, but several gaps remain:
- The design system and main pages exist, but the experience is not yet polished to production standard.
- Form accessibility still needs improvement, especially explicit labels, validation messaging, and better keyboard support.
- Some auth and navigation flows still show state-management or consistency issues.
- Mobile responsiveness and broader accessibility testing are still listed as pending work.
- Error handling and monitoring are improved, but external reporting and deeper reliability hardening are still incomplete.

### 3) Advertiser / business dashboard features
This area is also not fully finished:
- The business/advertiser routes and dashboard pages exist, but the full advertiser experience is still mostly a scaffold.
- Campaign creation/editing flows are present, but the full end-to-end workflow for launch, review, approvals, budget control, and reporting is not fully completed.
- The docs describe the advertiser-side campaign engine as a major planned domain, not a finished implementation.
- In short, the platform has the skeleton of an advertiser portal, but not the fully complete operational dashboard expected for real usage.

### 4) Cross-cutting completion gaps
A few blockers remain across the whole site:
- Supabase database migrations and RLS policies still need to be fully applied and verified.
- Test coverage is still too limited for production confidence.
- Environment configuration and deployment secrets are not fully hardened yet.
- The system is still closer to an advanced prototype than a fully launched platform.

## Bottom line

The website has:
- a strong base structure,
- many planned features already routed and partially implemented,
- but it is still missing full completion in:
  - admin dashboard operations,
  - polished UI/UX,
  - and advertiser/business dashboard functionality.

If you want, I can turn this into a prioritized checklist of “what to complete first” for the admin, UI, and advertiser areas.
