## Best insertion point

The strongest place to add this is the existing admin user-management flow in UsersManagementPage.tsx, not a brand-new feature area.

### Why this is the right spot
- It is already the central admin surface for user state, including plan assignment.
- It is already wired into the admin router at index.tsx, so it fits naturally into the current admin experience.
- The current codebase already has the right supporting layers:
  - plan updates in auth.ts
  - withdrawal enforcement and hold logic in wallet.ts

### Recommended structure
1. Extend the existing admin user panel to manage membership as:
   - Free membership
   - Paid membership
   - Paid plan variants if you want more granularity later

2. Keep the business rule in one place:
   - Free members can participate in tasks and other platform activity
   - Free members cannot withdraw funds
   - Paid members can withdraw according to their plan rules

3. Enforce that rule in the wallet/payment path, not only in the UI, so the restriction is reliable.

### Bottom line
Use the existing admin “Users” management area as the primary insertion point, and connect it to the current plan-update and wallet-policy flow already present in the codebase. That gives you the cleanest, most maintainable implementation.
